Sources - 

CBS (CORE BANKING SYSTEM)
Snowflake (cloud data sharing )
Argus SFTP(Secure file transfer protocol)
Aws s3 (cloud data sharing )
Azure Blob Storage(cloud data sharing )
The Argus API Cloud 
 Argus Direct (Excel or csv)
(Data store in Data lake or a big data warehouse)
Oracle (in this company's case) is the Source Database 
The "Input" Store: Where their reporters and analysts type in price assessments. This is usually a highly secure, transactional relational database (like Oracle or PostgreSQL).
The "History" Store: They have decades of data. This is often stored in a Data Lake or a Big Data warehouse (like Snowflake or BigQuery) because it contains millions of rows of historical price points.
The "Cache" Store: For real-time news and "tickers," they use in-memory storage (like Redis) so that the news hits your screen the second an analyst hits "publish."
—----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Extract - In this we identify data that we need, we pull it out and we don't change anything . It's going to be like a source system so the extract has one like a source system, so the extract has only one task to identify the data you have to pull out from the source and to not change anything, so we do not manipulate the data at all , it can stay as it is.

Transform - We will take this extracted data  and we are going to change the shape of the data and this process is really heavy work. We can do alot of stuff like ‘’ cleaning , data integration and formatting , normalization.


Load - In this we will take new data and we are going to insert it into targets . That means we going to take this prepared data from transformation step and move it into final destination ‘ data warehouse.
