=========================================================
                                       Creating DataWarehouse
=========================================================


USE master;
GO

-- Drop and recreate the 'DataWarehouse' database
IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.databases WHERE name = 'DataWarehouse')
BEGIN
    ALTER DATABASE DataWarehouse SET SINGLE_USER WITH ROLLBACK IMMEDIATE;
    DROP DATABASE DataWarehouse;
END;
GO
  
-- Create the Database 'DataWarehouse'

CREATE DATABASE DataWarehouse;
GO

USE DataWarehouse;
GO

-- CREATE Schemas
  
CREATE SCHEMA bronze;
GO
  
CREATE SCHEMA silver;
GO
  
CREATE SCHEMA gold;
GO

=========================================================
                                               Bronze Layer
=========================================================



Asking the right question will help you to design correct scripts in order to extract data and to avoid a lot of mistakes and challenges.
========================================================================

Most common question to ask 

========================================================================

We start by understanding the business context and the ownership
And would like to understand the story behind the data

— Who owns the data?
(who is responsible for the data, which it departments and so on)
— What business process does it supports?
(like customer transactions, supply chain logistics or may be finance reporting) With that you understand the importance of data.
— System and data documentation?
(having system documentation from the source is about learning materials about your data and it going to save a lot of time later when you are working or designing new data models 
—- Data model and data catalog
Description of the columns and the tables its going to be nice to have data catalog thios can help you alot in data warehouse , how you going to join the tables together.
So with that you find solid foundations about business context, processes and ownership of data


